, Play T5, Play W8, Play B3, Play B5.\nThe followings are your valid actions:[Play T7; Play T9; Play W7; Play W6; Play W5; Play T5; Play J1; Play B6; Play W4]\u3002", "reasoning": "", "output": "Evaluation: Hand: [W4, W5, W6, W7, W7, T5, T7, T9, B6, B6, J1]. Melds: Chow [T6, T7, T8] (exposed).  \nCurrent hand is incomplete (11 tiles + 3 in meld = 14 total). Need to form a winning hand (4 melds + pair).  \nPotential directions:  \n1. **All Simples / Half Flush / Full Flush?** Tiles are mixed suits (W, T, B, J). Not suited for Full Flush. Could aim for Half Flush (W suit + honors) but have T and B tiles.  \n2. **Look for meld opportunities:**  \n   - Pair candidates: W7 (2), B6 (2), others singles.  \n   - Potential sequences: W4,W5,W6 is a chow (need W4? Already have one W4). W5,W6,W7 possible with W5,W6,W7 (have W5,W6,W7,W7). Could form chow W5,W6,W7 and keep W7 pair.  \n   - Tiles: T5,T7,T9 are scattered; T7 used in exposed chow, so T5,T9 are isolated.  \n   - Honor J1 is single.  \n3. **Unshown tiles count:**  \n   - W7: 4 left (we have 2, total 4 in deck, so 2 left).  \n   - B6: 3 left (we have 2, total 3, so 1 left).  \n   - T7: 2 left (we have 1 in hand? Actually T7 in exposed meld, our hand has T7? No, hand shows T7:1 but we have T7 in hand? From valid actions, we can play T7, so yes we have one T7 in hand. But T7 is part of exposed chow [T6,T7,T8], so maybe that T7 is from hand? In meld, it's T6,T7,T8, we used T7 from hand? Actually \"Chi T7\" in our history means we claimed T7 to complete chow, so T7 is not in hand. Hand listing shows T7:1, so we have another T7 tile. So total T7: we have 1 in hand, 2 left unshown.  \n   - Other tiles: Many mid-range numbers available.  \n4. **Discard strategy:** Aim to keep flexibility and move toward tenpai.  \n   - **Isolated honors/low-value terminals:** J1 (single dragon), T9 (terminal), T5 (simple but isolated), T7 (isolated, though can pair with T7 from meld? Not really).  \n   - **Potential sequences:** W4,W5,W6 chow